# 🧠 3. THE MOST IMPORTANT INTERVIEW QUESTION

## "How do you decide which algorithm to use?"

Don't say:

> "I remember this problem."

Instead:

> **"I look at the constraints and structural properties of the input. For example, sorted data suggests binary search or two pointers, contiguous ranges suggest sliding window or prefix sums, top-K requirements suggest a heap, and repeated choices or overlapping subproblems suggest dynamic programming."**

That demonstrates **transferable problem-solving ability**.

